{"name":"Big Stone Beach","hex":"#886e54","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"big","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Biangai."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of great size, large.","Fat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/big"},{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"},{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Big Stone Lake","blocks":[{"text":"Big Stone Lake is a long, narrow freshwater lake and reservoir on the border between western Minnesota and northeastern South Dakota in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Big_Stone_Lake_from_Ortonville.JPG/330px-Big_Stone_Lake_from_Ortonville.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Stone_Lake","wikidata":"Q859342"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple 